# Hull grab in zero g: with the jetpack on, a grip with the hand on a hull takes hold of it, pushing the hand away from the
# hull moves the astronaut the other way, and letting go of the grip lets go.
# World: Green Station (survival; an asteroid base; the astronaut starts on foot in it). The test goes out into open space
# and builds an armor block 1.7 m ahead (a 2.5 m cube, its near face 45 cm ahead of the astronaut) with creative tools. The hand is put
# 45 cm ahead of the head, on the block's near face (the grab reaches 8 cm).
plugin SpaceEngineersVR
world game:Green Station
# zero g: the station's artificial gravity off
switch GravityGenerator off
switch GravityGeneratorSphere off
admin creativeTools
# out of the station into open space, nothing built within 10 m, to build there
goto open
build LargeBlockArmorBlock 3 as Test hull
# stand with the near face 45 cm ahead (the cube is 2.5 m: its centre 1.7 m away)
goto Test hull 1.7
log SpaceEngineersVR.log
expect session focused within 60

head 0 1.6 0
wait 2

# the jetpack on (the astronaut starts with it on in the station): a hull is only grabbed while floating
read character
expect jetpack == true

# before: nothing gripped
expect no log Hull grab: Right hand takes hold
read character
mark
wait 1
read character
expect position moved < 0.2

# the right hand on the hull, grip: it takes hold
hand right 0.2 1.2 -0.45
wait 0.7
press right grip
wait 1
expect log Hull grab: Right hand takes hold of within 5

# the hand pushed 20 cm into the hull: the astronaut is moved the other way
read character
mark
hand right 0.2 1.2 -0.55
wait 0.3
hand right 0.2 1.2 -0.65
wait 1
read character
expect position moved > 0.1

# the grip let go
release right grip
wait 1
expect log Hull grab: Right hand lets go of within 5
